      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In spinal trauma patients SSEPs were studied under median carpal nerve stimulation. In cases with pain syndrome, late SSEP waves (180-280 ms) were more pronounced as related to control group of patients without pain and to normal subjects. Psychoemotional personality scaling (MMPI) revealed the increased levels in the first three scales (s.c. \"neurotic triad\") in the pain group. A correlation was found between the late (P227) SSEP waves and the \"neurotic triad\" in MMPI."},
